CASE 4: MICROSERVICES ARCHITECTURE WITH CDN, API GATEWAY AND LOAD BALANCERS
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Suppose ek microservices architecture hai jisme multiple services hain,
har service ke multiple instances hain, har service ke paas apna Load Balancer hai,
aur URL routing ke liye API Gateway bhi hai.

Ab system ko optimize karne ke liye CDN add kiya ja sakta hai.

CDN ka full form hai Content Delivery Network.

CDNs geographically distributed servers hote hain jo different
geographical locations (e.g. Mumbai, Singapore, London, Virginia)
me deployed hote hain.

In geographical deployment locations ko CDN Edge Locations bola jata hai.

CDN ka primary purpose frequently requested content ko user ke
nearby CDN Edge se serve karna hota hai.



## MAIN BENEFITS OF CDN
--------------------------

1. Static content ko cache karna.

Examples:

    - Images
    - Videos
    - CSS files
    - JavaScript files
    - Fonts
    - Public static files


Iske benefits:

    1. Cached content CDN Edge se serve hota hai.

       Isliye Origin tak baar-baar request nahi jaati. 
       Origin = Wo original source jahan se CDN first time content fetch karta hai.

       Result:

           - Origin par unnecessary load reduce hota hai.


    2. CDN Edge generally user ke geographically nearby located hota hai.

       Isliye request ko har baar distant Origin tak
       travel nahi karna padta.

       Result:

           - Network latency reduce hoti hai.


    3. Reduced network latency ki wajah se response faster milta hai.


## NOTE:

Whether content should be cached and for how long
is generally controlled using HTTP caching headers
(e.g. Cache-Control, Expires).



## DNS AND CDN BEHAVIOUR
--------------------------

Case 4.1 : Anycast IP Based CDN

    Multiple CDN Edge Locations same IP address announce kar sakti hain.

    Ye same IP DNS me configured ho sakta hai.

    DNS resolution ke baad CDN ka IP return hota hai.

    Uske baad BGP routing automatically request ko
    nearest/optimal CDN Edge tak route karti hai.

    Example:

        User in India

            -> Nearby CDN Edge
               (e.g. Mumbai / Singapore)

        User in US

            -> Nearby CDN Edge
               (e.g. Virginia)

    User ko generally pata bhi nahi hota
    ki request kis CDN Edge ne serve ki.

    Network routing automatically
    appropriate CDN Edge select karti hai.



Case 4.2 : Geo DNS Based CDN

    Different CDN Edge Locations ke different IP addresses
    ho sakte hain.

    DNS resolver user ki approximate geographical location
    ke basis par nearby CDN IP return kar sakta hai.

    Example:

        User India me hai

            DNS returns India / Singapore CDN IP


        User Europe me hai

            DNS returns Europe CDN IP


## REQUEST FLOW
------------------


                    User
                      |
                      v
                     DNS
                      |
                      | returns CDN IP
                      v
               Nearby CDN Edge
                      |
          -----------------------------
          |                           |
          | Cache Hit                 | Cache Miss
          |                           |
          |                           v
          |                     API Gateway
          |                           |
          |          -----------------------------------
          |          |                 |               |
          |          v                 v               v
          |     User Service LB   Order Service LB  Payment Service LB
          |          |                 |               |
          |          v                 v               v
          |     User Instances   Order Instances  Payment Instances
          |
          |
          +-----------------------------> Response returned directly from CDN



Cache Hit:

    Requested content already available
    at the CDN Edge.

    Response directly CDN se serve ho jata hai.

    Origin ko request nahi jaati.



Cache Miss:

    Requested content CDN Edge par available nahi hota.

    CDN Origin se content fetch karta hai.

    Response client ko return karta hai.

    Saath hi content future requests ke liye
    CDN Edge par cache bhi kar leta hai.




## WHY CDN HELPS
-----------------

Suppose ek image repeatedly same geographical region
se request ho rahi hai.


Without CDN:

Har User request Origin tak travel karegi.


With CDN:

First Request:

        User Request

            ↓

         Nearest CDN Edge

            ↓

        Cache Miss

            ↓

         Origin

            ↓

        Image fetched

            ↓

        Cached at that CDN Edge.

            ↓

        Response returned


Subsequent Requests (from the same geographical region):

         User Request

            ↓

         Nearest CDN Edge

            ↓

         Cache Hit

            ↓

        Image directly returned

Origin ko request nahi jaati.

 
